MID_SCXX_02_01_m01: <EDH>
MID_SCXX_02_01_m01_001: You really think the thieves are holed up here?
MID_SCXX_02_01_m01_002: Legend has it Yu Phas purified herself here when\njoining the Dagda pantheon as Lord Solel's wife.
MID_SCXX_02_01_m01_003: Its remote location makes it an ideal place for\ntheir hideout.
MID_SCXX_02_01_m01_004: Not only have they stolen a statue honoring Saramis,\nthey dare to invade one of Yu Phas's holy sites.
MID_SCXX_02_01_m01_005: These reprehensible thieves shall breathe their last\ntoday. When I find them, I'll have their heads.
MID_SCXX_02_01_m01_043: 
MID_SCXX_02_01_m01_045: 
MID_SCXX_02_01_m01_046: 
MID_SCXX_02_01_m01_047: 
MID_SCXX_02_01_m01_048: 
MID_SCXX_02_01_m01_006: I hear you, boss, but you've gotta cool it. If you lose\ncontrol, we won't be able to hold you back.
MID_SCXX_02_01_m01_007: {SetColor=Gray}Ugh. I dunno if it's the arm or everything else going\non, but the boss has been so grouchy lately.{SetColor=Default}
MID_SCXX_02_01_m01_008: Aaaaaah!
MID_SCXX_02_01_m01_010: Shall we go?
MID_SCXX_02_01_m01_012: 
MID_SCXX_02_01_m01_013: 
MID_SCXX_02_01_m01_014: 
MID_SCXX_02_01_m01_015: 
MID_SCXX_02_01_m01_016: You gotta help me! My friends are dead!
MID_SCXX_02_01_m01_017: I see fragments at your feet. Are they what remain\nof the Saraminian warrior statue?
MID_SCXX_02_01_m01_018: Who gives a damn about the statue? We were only\nafter the jewel.
MID_SCXX_02_01_m01_019: We stole the statue just for that pretty blue thing.\nFigured it would fetch a high price.
MID_SCXX_02_01_m01_020: Your Majesty, this woman has admitted to being\na part of the gang of thieves.
MID_SCXX_02_01_m01_021: So they destroyed the statue in order to pilfer the\njewel. Such wanton disrespect.
MID_SCXX_02_01_m01_022: You will tell me what became of this jewel.
MID_SCXX_02_01_m01_023: We found some old shrine. Seemed like the perfect\nhiding spot, so we stashed it there.
MID_SCXX_02_01_m01_024: Can't fence a haul until the heat dies down, y'know.\nWe were gonna wait awhile before fetching it.
MID_SCXX_02_01_m01_025: But as soon as we stuck the jewel in there and shut\nthe door, a horde of monsters was on us!
MID_SCXX_02_01_m01_026: "Some old shrine"? Can it be that the purification\nshrine is still intact?!
MID_SCXX_02_01_m01_027: And you carelessly trespassed upon it?! You wicked\nheathens!
MID_SCXX_02_01_m01_028: Whoa, whoa, take it down a couple notches, Bona.\nEveryone's so riled up today.
MID_SCXX_02_01_m01_030: A horde of monsters? My boredom may be eased.
MID_SCXX_02_01_m01_032: 
MID_SCXX_02_01_m01_033: 
MID_SCXX_02_01_m01_034: 
MID_SCXX_02_01_m01_035: 
MID_SCXX_02_01_m01_036: Yes. Let us make for this shrine.
MID_SCXX_02_01_m01_037: Tobias, Bonaventure, bind this woman and hand\nher over to the temples.
MID_SCXX_02_01_m01_038: If she is the bait for an ambush, I trust you to handle\nany accomplices of hers.
MID_SCXX_02_01_m01_039: Will do, boss.
MID_SCXX_02_01_m01_040: Your Majesty, the tales speak of the shrine having\nunique defense mechanisms.
MID_SCXX_02_01_m01_041: I will tell you all I know of them, but be careful\nnonetheless. May you emerge victorious.
MID_SCXX_02_02_m01: <TH>
MID_SCXX_02_02_m01_001: The shrine is encased within a {SetColor=Gold}protective field{SetColor=Default}.\nThere should be {SetColor=Gold}mechanisms here to release it{SetColor=Default}.
MID_SCXX_02_02_m01_002: Bonaventure described a system of {SetColor=Gold}three devices\nin separate locations{SetColor=Default}.
MID_SCXX_02_02_m01_003: They apparently will only respond to the presence of\na {SetColor=Gold}living soul{SetColor=Default}. Everyone, call out if you find one.
MID_SCXX_02_02_m02: <TH>
MID_SCXX_02_02_m02_001: These golems and phantom soldiers must be the\nmonsters that thief spoke of.
MID_SCXX_02_02_m02_002: It pains me to destroy the defenders of one of\nYu Phas's holy sites.
MID_SCXX_02_02_m02_004: I cut through all obstacles.
MID_SCXX_02_02_m02_006: 
MID_SCXX_02_02_m02_007: 
MID_SCXX_02_02_m02_008: 
MID_SCXX_02_02_m02_009: 
MID_SCXX_02_02_m02_010: If there is no other way, then we shall cut\nthem down.
MID_SCXX_02_02_m04: <TH>
MID_SCXX_02_02_m04_001: Soldiers who do not live. Will I derive any pleasure\nfrom these?
MID_SCXX_02_02_m04_002: Take them seriously. They are lethal opponents.
MID_SCXX_02_02_m04_003: I hope so. Otherwise the fight is pointless.
MID_SCXX_02_02_m06: <TH>
MID_SCXX_02_02_m06_001: I looked for surviving thieves, but it seems the only\none still living is that one from before.
MID_SCXX_02_02_m06_002: You searched despite the fog? Your dedication is\nadmirable, White-Maned Demon.
MID_SCXX_02_02_m06_003: As I see it, lives that can be saved should be.
MID_SCXX_02_02_m07: <TH>
MID_SCXX_02_02_m07_001: There better be a mighty fine payout at the end\nof all this manual labor, Majesty...
MID_SCXX_02_02_m07_002: Enough buzzing, you mosquito. You shall drink your\nfill from our coffers.
MID_SCXX_02_02_m08: <TH>
MID_SCXX_02_02_m08_001: They're certainly being cranky after getting\nwoken from their slumber.
MID_SCXX_02_02_m08_002: Er...is that so? I confess I had not considered that\nperspective.
MID_SCXX_02_02_m09: <TH>
MID_SCXX_02_02_m09_001: I am delighted to repay the debt incurred by\nborrowing your ship, Theodora.
MID_SCXX_02_02_m09_002: Heh. It always comes down to debts between us.\nRegardless, I am grateful.
MID_SCXX_02_02_m10: <TH>
MID_SCXX_02_02_m10_001: That is a start. It is very like Yu Phas to require the\npresence of a soul.
MID_SCXX_02_02_m11: <TH>
MID_SCXX_02_02_m11_001: The second device is ready. It is an honor for Yu\nPhas to approve of one's soul.
MID_SCXX_02_02_m12: <TH>
MID_SCXX_02_02_m12_001: The field has been quelled. Well done, all of you.\nLet us proceed directly to the shrine.
MID_SCXX_02_03_m01: <EDH>
MID_SCXX_02_03_m01_001: So this is the interior of the shrine...and this must\nbe the jewel.
MID_SCXX_02_03_m01_002: Hello, Queen Theodora. You have our gratitude for\nyour help resolving this matter.
MID_SCXX_02_03_m01_070: 
MID_SCXX_02_03_m01_072: 
MID_SCXX_02_03_m01_073: 
MID_SCXX_02_03_m01_074: 
MID_SCXX_02_03_m01_075: 
MID_SCXX_02_03_m01_003: I came to tell you what we learned from interrogating\nthe thief.
MID_SCXX_02_03_m01_004: I doubt she had any testimony worth hearing. After\nall, they knew nothing of the statue's significance.
MID_SCXX_02_03_m01_005: You are correct. They had no knowledge of what\nit was they stole.
MID_SCXX_02_03_m01_006: Their ignorance isn't surprising, given how few\npeople in Dagsion worship Yu Phas.
MID_SCXX_02_03_m01_007: That much I knew. I did not come here to lodge a\ncomplaint over religious differences.
MID_SCXX_02_03_m01_008: That's very generous of you. I hate to admit this,\nas a priest of the temples...
MID_SCXX_02_03_m01_009: But that shrine has been long neglected. Its interior\nwas empty and the door was left open.
MID_SCXX_02_03_m01_010: Unbelievable carelessness. Anyone could have used\nit for any ill purpose they chose.
MID_SCXX_02_03_m01_011: Worse, that thing was a death trap waiting to be\nsprung. Did you see all those things that came out?
MID_SCXX_02_03_m01_012: I wouldn't go that far. Under normal circumstances,\nit would have held up to a bit of tampering.
MID_SCXX_02_03_m01_013: The disaster you saw today was the result of a few\ncoincidences all piling up.
MID_SCXX_02_03_m01_014: To begin with, the jewel they took from the warrior\nstatue was a relic of Yu Phas.
MID_SCXX_02_03_m01_015: Ahh, I see. And then the thieves brought it to\na shrine dedicated to Yu Phas.
MID_SCXX_02_03_m01_016: That must have activated the mechanism protecting\nthe shrine. I see what you mean.
MID_SCXX_02_03_m01_017: The jewel is called the Seafarer's Gleam. It was a gift\nto your people from Lord Solel.
MID_SCXX_02_03_m01_018: It has the colors of the sea, so he thought it suited\nthe seafaring Saraminians.
MID_SCXX_02_03_m01_019: It was a mark of his gratitude for your valor, as well\nas your continued reverence for his beloved Yu Phas.
MID_SCXX_02_03_m01_020: So it wasn't some ordinary jewel, huh? Wish we'd\nknown that sooner.
MID_SCXX_02_03_m01_021: The Divine Sovereign was pretty slick, keeping quiet\nabout something we'd have been thrilled to see.
MID_SCXX_02_03_m01_022: Indeed, to receive a relic of Yu Phas is a great honor\nfor us Saraminians.
MID_SCXX_02_03_m01_023: It is fitting that it was a part of the statue, to better\nhonor the souls of those brave warriors.
MID_SCXX_02_03_m01_024: But there is still the question of how such a precious\nrelic came to be left out in the open.
MID_SCXX_02_03_m01_025: Well, it was fixed pretty firmly in that statue. And it\nlooked like an ordinary decoration.
MID_SCXX_02_03_m01_026: We never considered that someone might steal the\nstatue and smash it apart to get the jewel.
MID_SCXX_02_03_m01_027: But hindsight isn't much of an excuse for losing\nyour precious warrior statue.
MID_SCXX_02_03_m01_028: Again, we deeply apologize. We'll have a sculptor\nmake a fitting replacement.
MID_SCXX_02_03_m01_029: One made of tougher, heavier material so it can't\nbe carted off or destroyed.
MID_SCXX_02_03_m01_030: As for the Seafarer's Gleam...we think you should\nhold on to it, Queen Theodora.
MID_SCXX_02_03_m01_031: Are you certain?
MID_SCXX_02_03_m01_032: Yes. The Divine Sovereign himself said so, to show\nhis gratitude and respect for your proud people.
MID_SCXX_02_03_m01_033: Very well. Inform Lord Solel that I accept, and\nconvey my thanks.
MID_SCXX_02_03_m01_034: Don't worry about the shrine. The temples will take\ncare of it. And with that, I should take my leave.
MID_SCXX_02_03_m01_036: Is that all?
MID_SCXX_02_03_m01_038: 
MID_SCXX_02_03_m01_039: 
MID_SCXX_02_03_m01_040: 
MID_SCXX_02_03_m01_041: 
MID_SCXX_02_03_m01_042: Yes. I appreciate your helping me with this. I have\na reward for your fine work.
MID_SCXX_02_03_m01_045: I will go. Call on me again if you find a\nworthwhile opponent.
MID_SCXX_02_03_m01_047: 
MID_SCXX_02_03_m01_048: 
MID_SCXX_02_03_m01_049: 
MID_SCXX_02_03_m01_050: 
MID_SCXX_02_03_m01_051: I incurred a debt today. I hope the time comes when\nI can repay it.
MID_SCXX_02_03_m01_052: How do you figure? I mean, you gave 'em a reward.\nThat oughta be enough, boss.
MID_SCXX_02_03_m01_054: That aside, Your Majesty, I ought to bring something\nto your attention.
MID_SCXX_02_03_m01_055: If my eyes do not deceive me, the wavelike pattern\non that jewel is shifting.
MID_SCXX_02_03_m01_056: So it is. I do not recall that happening before I held\nit in my right hand.
MID_SCXX_02_03_m01_057: I find it soothing somehow. How can this be?
MID_SCXX_02_03_m01_058: The relic did once belong to Yu Phas. Perhaps it is\nendowed with her blessing.
MID_SCXX_02_03_m01_059: Whatever it is, the effect must be suppressing the\ncurse you bear.
MID_SCXX_02_03_m01_060: That's great! Now we don't gotta worry about Her\nMajesty flying off the handle again.
MID_SCXX_02_03_m01_061: Hold your tongue, Tobias. Do you not appreciate the\ndepth of Her Majesty's suffering?
MID_SCXX_02_03_m01_062: Be at ease, Bonaventure. I know I have caused the\ntwo of you much trouble.
MID_SCXX_02_03_m01_063: It is an honor beyond compare to be so blessed\nby Yu Phas.
MID_SCXX_02_03_m01_064: I would say so whether or not the Seafarer's Gleam\ntruly suppresses the curse.
MID_SCXX_02_03_m01_065: Sure, it does. Why else would the jewel fall into your\nlap like that, boss?
MID_SCXX_02_03_m01_066: The souls of Saraminian warriors, moved to save\ntheir queen... Perhaps it was meant to be.
MID_SCXX_02_03_m01_067: Hm. I should like to think so.
MID_SCXX_02_03_m01_068: We owe our good fortune to the honorable warriors\nof Saramis...as well as those from elsewhere.